  "note": "First election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council under the 1922 wards, polled Monday 15 January 1923. The South Ward's five members were returned unopposed; the North Ward's seven seats were contested by eight candidates (Belfast News-Letter, 17 January 1923, p. 6). Eight candidates for seven seats. Image-read in BNL 17 Jan 1923 p. 6 and Northern Whig 17 Jan 1923 p. 6 (same type): M'Alister 283 (Irish News block also 283; corrected from 286); David Henry printed (L.U.) in the result (U. in the nomination list). Capt. Lyle's figure is blurred as 2?7 in every copy (207 or 267). The paper prints the seven elected in strict descending order (299, 283, 271, Lyle, 261, 253, 227); only 267 keeps that order (207 would fall below Ekin's 227), so 267 is recorded (corrected from 207). Lyle is elected on either reading, since the defeated candidate had 177 (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026)."
